## What a `type: linkset` instance is

A first-class representation of INTER-DATASET TYPED CROSS-LINK METADATA — analog of `void:Linkset` from the VoID vocabulary.  A linkset declares: "FROM this dataset, USING this predicate, TO that target dataset — N typed-edges of this shape exist."  Linksets are the substrate's mechanism for federating typed-edge graphs across dataset boundaries while keeping cross-dataset reference metadata first-class + queryable.

## When to materialize a linkset

- Cross-dataset typed-edges exist (e.g., memorial in dataset A cites memorial in dataset B)
- Federation discovery needs to enumerate available cross-references
- Audit invariants need to track cross-dataset reference health (broken-link detection at federation scale)

